    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Employee -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Employee">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#LivingPerson"/>
                    <owl:Class>
                        <owl:unionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Adolescent"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Adult"/>
                            <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Elderly"/>
                        </owl:unionOf>
                    </owl:Class>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeCommitment -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeCommitment">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#IntrinsicMode"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#inheresIn"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Employee"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#isAspectualFactorOf"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeInfluencedRetentionContext"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeConsequenceContext -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeConsequenceContext">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#ConsequenceContext"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty>
                    <rdf:Description>
                        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#broughtAbout"/>
                    </rdf:Description>
                </owl:onProperty>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#InvoluntaryTurnover"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#hasConsequenceElement"/>
                <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#ConcreteIndividual"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">All post-state situations representing the personal, psychological, and financial outcomes (both positive and negative) experienced by an employee following a turnover or retention event.

OntoTurnover/gUFO application: This is a specialization of :ConsequenceContext (gufo:Situation). It groups employee-side post-action situations. Concrete consequence elements are connected by :hasConsequenceElement rather than declared as subclasses of the context. The subtype hierarchy below this class contains only more specific context classes.

Synonyms: employee outcome context; worker consequence situation; employee post-event situation; employee outcome state of affairs; Worker Consequence Context; Staff Consequence Context; Workforce Consequence Context

References:
- Enander, A., &amp; Cardoso, J. (2020). How is employee turnover related to employee retention? A systematic review on two sets of meta-analyses [Dissertação de mestrado, Lund University]. Lund University Publications. http://lup.lub.lu.se/student-papers/record/9022943/file/9022946.pdf
- Almeida, J. P. A., Guizzardi, G., Sales, T. P., &amp; Falbo, R. A. (2019). gUFO: A Lightweight Implementation of the Unified Foundational Ontology (UFO). https://nemo-ufes.github.io/gufo/
- Guizzardi, R., Carneiro, B. G., Porello, D., &amp; Guizzardi, G. (2020). A core ontology on decision making. CEUR Workshop Proceedings, 2728, 9–21. https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2728/paper1.pdf</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeInfluencedRetentionContext -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeInfluencedRetentionContext">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#RetentionMotivatingContext"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Individual states, active adjustments, and coping mechanisms driven directly by the employee that contribute to their decision to stay.

OntoTurnover/gUFO application: A gufo:Situation context collecting relevant concrete factors through :hasContextualFactor (inverse :isContextualFactorOf). The factors retain their own direct gUFO superclasses and are not subclasses of this context. When an actual contribution is established, this situation may be related by gufo:contributedToTrigger to :StayDecisionMakingEvent. The universal restriction constrains possible targets without asserting that every risk or retention context necessarily produces a decision. Employee and employer influences can coexist in one retention context.

Synonyms: employee-driven retention context; worker-influenced staying context; employee-shaped retention situation; employee-led continuance context; Worker Influenced Retention Context; Staff Influenced Retention Context; Workforce Influenced Retention Context

References:
- Enander, A., &amp; Cardoso, J. (2020). How is employee turnover related to employee retention? A systematic review on two sets of meta-analyses [Dissertação de mestrado, Lund University]. Lund University Publications. http://lup.lub.lu.se/student-papers/record/9022943/file/9022946.pdf
- Almeida, J. P. A., Guizzardi, G., Sales, T. P., &amp; Falbo, R. A. (2019). gUFO: A Lightweight Implementation of the Unified Foundational Ontology (UFO). https://nemo-ufes.github.io/gufo/
- Guizzardi, R., Carneiro, B. G., Porello, D., &amp; Guizzardi, G. (2020). A core ontology on decision making. CEUR Workshop Proceedings, 2728, 9–21. https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2728/paper1.pdf</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeInvoluntaryTurnoverConsequenceContext -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeInvoluntaryTurnoverConsequenceContext">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeConsequenceContext"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gufo:Situation that classifies post-state situations representing the negative personal, financial, and psychological outcomes experienced by an employee after an employer-initiated termination event.

OntoTurnover/gUFO application: This class specializes :EmployeeConsequenceContext, hence gufo:Situation. It is a consequence context brought about by :InvoluntaryTurnover, with elements connected by :hasConsequenceElement (inverse :isConsequenceElementOf). Concrete consequence classes specialize their gUFO categories rather than this context. Employee-side and employer-side contexts can remain distinct individuals even when brought about by the same action.

Synonyms: employee involuntary-separation outcome context; worker dismissal consequence context; employee discharge outcome situation; employee layoff consequence context; Worker Involuntary Turnover Consequence Context; Staff Involuntary Turnover Consequence Context; Workforce Involuntary Turnover Consequence Context

References:
- Enander, A., &amp; Cardoso, J. (2020). How is employee turnover related to employee retention? A systematic review on two sets of meta-analyses [Dissertação de mestrado, Lund University]. Lund University Publications. http://lup.lub.lu.se/student-papers/record/9022943/file/9022946.pdf
- Santana, A. C., Rodrigues, C. M. de O., Farias Junior, I. H. de, &amp; Santos, W. B. (2023). OntoTurnover: A lightweight domain ontology for modeling employee turnover. In 2023 18th Iberian Conference on Information Systems and Technologies (CISTI) (pp. 1–4). IEEE. https://doi.org/10.23919/CISTI58278.2023.10211799
- Santana, A. C., Farias Junior, I. H. de, Santos, W. B., &amp; Rodrigues, C. M. de O. (2023). OntoTurnover: Uma ontologia de domínio sobre a rotatividade de profissionais. In Anais Estendidos do XXII Simpósio Brasileiro de Qualidade de Software (pp. 13–18). Sociedade Brasileira de Computação. https://doi.org/10.5753/sbqsestendido.2023.235887
- Almeida, J. P. A., Guizzardi, G., Sales, T. P., &amp; Falbo, R. A. (2019). gUFO: A Lightweight Implementation of the Unified Foundational Ontology (UFO). https://nemo-ufes.github.io/gufo/
- Guizzardi, R., Carneiro, B. G., Porello, D., &amp; Guizzardi, G. (2020). A core ontology on decision making. CEUR Workshop Proceedings, 2728, 9–21. https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2728/paper1.pdf</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeRetentionConsequenceContext -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeRetentionConsequenceContext">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeConsequenceContext"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty>
                    <rdf:Description>
                        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#broughtAbout"/>
                    </rdf:Description>
                </owl:onProperty>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Retention"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#hasConsequenceElement"/>
                <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#ConcreteIndividual"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gufo:Situation that classifies post-state situations representing the positive personal and professional outcomes experienced by an employee who remains with their current employer.

OntoTurnover/gUFO application: This class specializes :EmployeeConsequenceContext, hence gufo:Situation. It is a consequence context brought about by :Retention, with elements connected by :hasConsequenceElement (inverse :isConsequenceElementOf). Concrete consequence classes specialize their gUFO categories rather than this context. Employee-side and employer-side contexts can remain distinct individuals even when brought about by the same action.

Synonyms: employee retention outcome context; worker staying consequence context; employee continuance outcome situation; employee retention post-state; Worker Retention Consequence Context; Staff Retention Consequence Context; Workforce Retention Consequence Context

References:
- Enander, A., &amp; Cardoso, J. (2020). How is employee turnover related to employee retention? A systematic review on two sets of meta-analyses [Dissertação de mestrado, Lund University]. Lund University Publications. http://lup.lub.lu.se/student-papers/record/9022943/file/9022946.pdf
- Santana, A. C., Rodrigues, C. M. de O., Farias Junior, I. H. de, &amp; Santos, W. B. (2023). OntoTurnover: A lightweight domain ontology for modeling employee turnover. In 2023 18th Iberian Conference on Information Systems and Technologies (CISTI) (pp. 1–4). IEEE. https://doi.org/10.23919/CISTI58278.2023.10211799
- Santana, A. C., Farias Junior, I. H. de, Santos, W. B., &amp; Rodrigues, C. M. de O. (2023). OntoTurnover: Uma ontologia de domínio sobre a rotatividade de profissionais. In Anais Estendidos do XXII Simpósio Brasileiro de Qualidade de Software (pp. 13–18). Sociedade Brasileira de Computação. https://doi.org/10.5753/sbqsestendido.2023.235887
- Almeida, J. P. A., Guizzardi, G., Sales, T. P., &amp; Falbo, R. A. (2019). gUFO: A Lightweight Implementation of the Unified Foundational Ontology (UFO). https://nemo-ufes.github.io/gufo/
- Guizzardi, R., Carneiro, B. G., Porello, D., &amp; Guizzardi, G. (2020). A core ontology on decision making. CEUR Workshop Proceedings, 2728, 9–21. https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2728/paper1.pdf</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeVoluntaryTurnoverConsequenceContext -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeVoluntaryTurnoverConsequenceContext">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeConsequenceContext"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty>
                    <rdf:Description>
                        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#broughtAbout"/>
                    </rdf:Description>
                </owl:onProperty>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#VoluntaryTurnover"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#hasConsequenceElement"/>
                <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#ConcreteIndividual"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gufo:Situation that classifies post-state situations representing the personal, professional, and financial changes (both positive and negative) experienced by an employee after resigning from their role.

OntoTurnover/gUFO application: This class specializes :EmployeeConsequenceContext, hence gufo:Situation. It is a consequence context brought about by :VoluntaryTurnover, with elements connected by :hasConsequenceElement (inverse :isConsequenceElementOf). Concrete consequence classes specialize their gUFO categories rather than this context. Employee-side and employer-side contexts can remain distinct individuals even when brought about by the same action.

Synonyms: employee voluntary-exit outcome context; worker resignation consequence context; employee quit outcome situation; employee voluntary-separation post-state; Worker Voluntary Turnover Consequence Context; Staff Voluntary Turnover Consequence Context; Workforce Voluntary Turnover Consequence Context

References:
- Enander, A., &amp; Cardoso, J. (2020). How is employee turnover related to employee retention? A systematic review on two sets of meta-analyses [Dissertação de mestrado, Lund University]. Lund University Publications. http://lup.lub.lu.se/student-papers/record/9022943/file/9022946.pdf
- Santana, A. C., Rodrigues, C. M. de O., Farias Junior, I. H. de, &amp; Santos, W. B. (2023). OntoTurnover: A lightweight domain ontology for modeling employee turnover. In 2023 18th Iberian Conference on Information Systems and Technologies (CISTI) (pp. 1–4). IEEE. https://doi.org/10.23919/CISTI58278.2023.10211799
- Santana, A. C., Farias Junior, I. H. de, Santos, W. B., &amp; Rodrigues, C. M. de O. (2023). OntoTurnover: Uma ontologia de domínio sobre a rotatividade de profissionais. In Anais Estendidos do XXII Simpósio Brasileiro de Qualidade de Software (pp. 13–18). Sociedade Brasileira de Computação. https://doi.org/10.5753/sbqsestendido.2023.235887
- Almeida, J. P. A., Guizzardi, G., Sales, T. P., &amp; Falbo, R. A. (2019). gUFO: A Lightweight Implementation of the Unified Foundational Ontology (UFO). https://nemo-ufes.github.io/gufo/
- Guizzardi, R., Carneiro, B. G., Porello, D., &amp; Guizzardi, G. (2020). A core ontology on decision making. CEUR Workshop Proceedings, 2728, 9–21. https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2728/paper1.pdf</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeWellBeing -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeWellBeing">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#IntrinsicMode"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#inheresIn"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Employee"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#isAspectualFactorOf"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployeeInfluencedRetentionContext"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Employer -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Employer">
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Agent"/>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty>
                            <rdf:Description>
                                <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#mediates"/>
                            </rdf:Description>
                        </owl:onProperty>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Employment"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployerConsequenceContext -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployerConsequenceContext">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#ConsequenceContext"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty>
                    <rdf:Description>
                        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#broughtAbout"/>
                    </rdf:Description>
                </owl:onProperty>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#InvoluntaryTurnover"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#hasConsequenceElement"/>
                <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#ConcreteIndividual"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A ConsequenceContext representing post-state consequences experienced by the employer after a turnover or retention event.

OntoTurnover/gUFO application: This is a specialization of :ConsequenceContext (gufo:Situation). It groups employer-side post-action situations. Concrete consequence elements are connected by :hasConsequenceElement rather than declared as subclasses of the context. The subtype hierarchy below this class contains only more specific context classes.

Synonyms: employer outcome context; organizational consequence situation; employer post-event situation; organizational outcome state of affairs; Organization Consequence Context; Company Consequence Context; Firm Consequence Context

References:
- Almeida, J. P. A., Guizzardi, G., Sales, T. P., &amp; Falbo, R. A. (2019). gUFO: A Lightweight Implementation of the Unified Foundational Ontology (UFO). https://nemo-ufes.github.io/gufo/
- Santana, A. C., Rodrigues, C. M. de O., Farias Junior, I. H. de, &amp; Santos, W. B. (2023). OntoTurnover: A lightweight domain ontology for modeling employee turnover. In 2023 18th Iberian Conference on Information Systems and Technologies (CISTI) (pp. 1–4). IEEE. https://doi.org/10.23919/CISTI58278.2023.10211799
- Enander, A., &amp; Cardoso, J. (2020). How is employee turnover related to employee retention? A systematic review on two sets of meta-analyses [Master&apos;s thesis, Lund University]. http://lup.lub.lu.se/student-papers/record/9022943/file/9022946.pdf
- Guizzardi, R., Carneiro, B. G., Porello, D., &amp; Guizzardi, G. (2020). A core ontology on decision making. CEUR Workshop Proceedings, 2728, 9–21. https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2728/paper1.pdf</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployerInfluencedRetentionContext -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployerInfluencedRetentionContext">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#RetentionMotivatingContext"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#contributedToTrigger"/>
                <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#StayDecisionMakingEvent"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#hasContextualFactor"/>
                <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#ConcreteIndividual"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Positive workplace situations and HR initiatives that are directly controlled and designed by the employing organization to foster retention.

OntoTurnover/gUFO application: A gufo:Situation context collecting relevant concrete factors through :hasContextualFactor (inverse :isContextualFactorOf). The factors retain their own direct gUFO superclasses and are not subclasses of this context. When an actual contribution is established, this situation may be related by gufo:contributedToTrigger to :StayDecisionMakingEvent. The universal restriction constrains possible targets without asserting that every risk or retention context necessarily produces a decision. Employee and employer influences can coexist in one retention context.

Synonyms: employer-driven retention context; organization-influenced staying context; management-shaped retention situation; organizational retention context; Organization Influenced Retention Context; Company Influenced Retention Context; Firm Influenced Retention Context

References:
- Enander, A., &amp; Cardoso, J. (2020). How is employee turnover related to employee retention? A systematic review on two sets of meta-analyses [Dissertação de mestrado, Lund University]. Lund University Publications. http://lup.lub.lu.se/student-papers/record/9022943/file/9022946.pdf
- Almeida, J. P. A., Guizzardi, G., Sales, T. P., &amp; Falbo, R. A. (2019). gUFO: A Lightweight Implementation of the Unified Foundational Ontology (UFO). https://nemo-ufes.github.io/gufo/
- Guizzardi, R., Carneiro, B. G., Porello, D., &amp; Guizzardi, G. (2020). A core ontology on decision making. CEUR Workshop Proceedings, 2728, 9–21. https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2728/paper1.pdf</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployerInvoluntaryTurnoverConsequenceContext -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployerInvoluntaryTurnoverConsequenceContext">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployerConsequenceContext"/>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gufo:Situation experienced by an employer as a result of involuntary employee exits.

OntoTurnover/gUFO application: This class specializes :EmployerConsequenceContext, hence gufo:Situation. It is a consequence context brought about by :InvoluntaryTurnover, with elements connected by :hasConsequenceElement (inverse :isConsequenceElementOf). Concrete consequence classes specialize their gUFO categories rather than this context. Employee-side and employer-side contexts can remain distinct individuals even when brought about by the same action.

Synonyms: employer involuntary-separation outcome context; organizational dismissal consequence context; employer discharge outcome situation; layoff consequence context; Organization Involuntary Turnover Consequence Context; Company Involuntary Turnover Consequence Context; Firm Involuntary Turnover Consequence Context

References:
- Enander, A., &amp; Cardoso, J. (2020). How is employee turnover related to employee retention? A systematic review on two sets of meta-analyses [Dissertação de mestrado, Lund University]. Lund University Publications. http://lup.lub.lu.se/student-papers/record/9022943/file/9022946.pdf
- Santana, A. C., Rodrigues, C. M. de O., Farias Junior, I. H. de, &amp; Santos, W. B. (2023). OntoTurnover: A lightweight domain ontology for modeling employee turnover. In 2023 18th Iberian Conference on Information Systems and Technologies (CISTI) (pp. 1–4). IEEE. https://doi.org/10.23919/CISTI58278.2023.10211799
- Santana, A. C., Farias Junior, I. H. de, Santos, W. B., &amp; Rodrigues, C. M. de O. (2023). OntoTurnover: Uma ontologia de domínio sobre a rotatividade de profissionais. In Anais Estendidos do XXII Simpósio Brasileiro de Qualidade de Software (pp. 13–18). Sociedade Brasileira de Computação. https://doi.org/10.5753/sbqsestendido.2023.235887
- Almeida, J. P. A., Guizzardi, G., Sales, T. P., &amp; Falbo, R. A. (2019). gUFO: A Lightweight Implementation of the Unified Foundational Ontology (UFO). https://nemo-ufes.github.io/gufo/
- Guizzardi, R., Carneiro, B. G., Porello, D., &amp; Guizzardi, G. (2020). A core ontology on decision making. CEUR Workshop Proceedings, 2728, 9–21. https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2728/paper1.pdf</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployerRetentionConsequenceContext -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployerRetentionConsequenceContext">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployerConsequenceContext"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty>
                    <rdf:Description>
                        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#broughtAbout"/>
                    </rdf:Description>
                </owl:onProperty>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Retention"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#hasConsequenceElement"/>
                <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#ConcreteIndividual"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gufo:Situation representing the positive organizational outcomes and benefits brought about by a successful retention event.

OntoTurnover/gUFO application: This class specializes :EmployerConsequenceContext, hence gufo:Situation. It is a consequence context brought about by :Retention, with elements connected by :hasConsequenceElement (inverse :isConsequenceElementOf). Concrete consequence classes specialize their gUFO categories rather than this context. Employee-side and employer-side contexts can remain distinct individuals even when brought about by the same action.

Synonyms: employer retention outcome context; organizational staying consequence context; workforce-continuance outcome situation; retention post-state for the employer; Organization Retention Consequence Context; Company Retention Consequence Context; Firm Retention Consequence Context

References:
- Enander, A., &amp; Cardoso, J. (2020). How is employee turnover related to employee retention? A systematic review on two sets of meta-analyses [Dissertação de mestrado, Lund University]. Lund University Publications. http://lup.lub.lu.se/student-papers/record/9022943/file/9022946.pdf
- Santana, A. C., Rodrigues, C. M. de O., Farias Junior, I. H. de, &amp; Santos, W. B. (2023). OntoTurnover: A lightweight domain ontology for modeling employee turnover. In 2023 18th Iberian Conference on Information Systems and Technologies (CISTI) (pp. 1–4). IEEE. https://doi.org/10.23919/CISTI58278.2023.10211799
- Santana, A. C., Farias Junior, I. H. de, Santos, W. B., &amp; Rodrigues, C. M. de O. (2023). OntoTurnover: Uma ontologia de domínio sobre a rotatividade de profissionais. In Anais Estendidos do XXII Simpósio Brasileiro de Qualidade de Software (pp. 13–18). Sociedade Brasileira de Computação. https://doi.org/10.5753/sbqsestendido.2023.235887
- Almeida, J. P. A., Guizzardi, G., Sales, T. P., &amp; Falbo, R. A. (2019). gUFO: A Lightweight Implementation of the Unified Foundational Ontology (UFO). https://nemo-ufes.github.io/gufo/
- Guizzardi, R., Carneiro, B. G., Porello, D., &amp; Guizzardi, G. (2020). A core ontology on decision making. CEUR Workshop Proceedings, 2728, 9–21. https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2728/paper1.pdf</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployerVoluntaryTurnoverConsequenceContext -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployerVoluntaryTurnoverConsequenceContext">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#EmployerConsequenceContext"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty>
                    <rdf:Description>
                        <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#broughtAbout"/>
                    </rdf:Description>
                </owl:onProperty>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#VoluntaryTurnover"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#hasConsequenceElement"/>
                <owl:allValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#ConcreteIndividual"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gufo:Situation that classifies negative post-state situations experienced by an employer following voluntary employee resignations.

OntoTurnover/gUFO application: This class specializes :EmployerConsequenceContext, hence gufo:Situation. It is a consequence context brought about by :VoluntaryTurnover, with elements connected by :hasConsequenceElement (inverse :isConsequenceElementOf). Concrete consequence classes specialize their gUFO categories rather than this context. Employee-side and employer-side contexts can remain distinct individuals even when brought about by the same action.

Synonyms: employer voluntary-exit outcome context; organizational resignation consequence context; quit-related employer outcome situation; voluntary-separation organizational post-state; Organization Voluntary Turnover Consequence Context; Company Voluntary Turnover Consequence Context; Firm Voluntary Turnover Consequence Context

References:
- Enander, A., &amp; Cardoso, J. (2020). How is employee turnover related to employee retention? A systematic review on two sets of meta-analyses [Dissertação de mestrado, Lund University]. Lund University Publications. http://lup.lub.lu.se/student-papers/record/9022943/file/9022946.pdf
- Santana, A. C., Rodrigues, C. M. de O., Farias Junior, I. H. de, &amp; Santos, W. B. (2023). OntoTurnover: A lightweight domain ontology for modeling employee turnover. In 2023 18th Iberian Conference on Information Systems and Technologies (CISTI) (pp. 1–4). IEEE. https://doi.org/10.23919/CISTI58278.2023.10211799
- Santana, A. C., Farias Junior, I. H. de, Santos, W. B., &amp; Rodrigues, C. M. de O. (2023). OntoTurnover: Uma ontologia de domínio sobre a rotatividade de profissionais. In Anais Estendidos do XXII Simpósio Brasileiro de Qualidade de Software (pp. 13–18). Sociedade Brasileira de Computação. https://doi.org/10.5753/sbqsestendido.2023.235887
- Almeida, J. P. A., Guizzardi, G., Sales, T. P., &amp; Falbo, R. A. (2019). gUFO: A Lightweight Implementation of the Unified Foundational Ontology (UFO). https://nemo-ufes.github.io/gufo/
- Guizzardi, R., Carneiro, B. G., Porello, D., &amp; Guizzardi, G. (2020). A core ontology on decision making. CEUR Workshop Proceedings, 2728, 9–21. https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2728/paper1.pdf</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Class>
    


    <!-- http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Employment -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Employment">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#Relator"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Class>
                <owl:intersectionOf rdf:parseType="Collection">
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#mediates"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Employee"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                    <owl:Restriction>
                        <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.org/nemo/gufo#mediates"/>
                        <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#Employer"/>
                    </owl:Restriction>
                </owl:intersectionOf>
            </owl:Class>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
    </owl:Class>
    


