    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#ManagementSupportToFun">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gufo:Situation representing a situation in which management encourages and sponsors enjoyable social activities at work.

In the context of the OntoTurnover domain, this situation is a potential employer-influenced retention factor. Its instances enter a EmployerInfluencedRetentionContext through :isSituationalFactorOf, a subproperty of gufo:isSituationProperPartOf and :isContextualFactorOf, and are therefore classified by the reasoner as RetentionPotentialFactor. The context, not the factor itself, may contribute to triggering a StayIntentionFormation (gufo:contributedToTrigger), and the property chain :contributedToFormationOf infers the resulting intention when one is recorded. Being a factor does not entail that an intention, a decision, or a retention actually occurs.

Examples include a company that funds monthly team gatherings.

Synonyms: Workplace Fun Initiatives; Social Engagement Support; Management Assistance to Fun; Management Backing to Fun; Management Help to Fun.

References:

Enander, A., &amp; Cardoso, J. (2020). How is employee turnover related to employee retention? A systematic review on two sets of meta-analyses [Dissertação de mestrado, Lund University]. Lund University Publications. http://lup.lub.lu.se/student-papers/record/9022943/file/9022946.pdf

Almeida, J. P. A., Guizzardi, G., Sales, T. P., &amp; Falbo, R. A. (2019). gUFO: A Lightweight Implementation of the Unified Foundational Ontology (UFO). https://nemo-ufes.github.io/gufo/

Guizzardi, R., Carneiro, B. G., Porello, D., &amp; Guizzardi, G. (2020). A core ontology on decision making. CEUR Workshop Proceedings, 2728, 9–21. https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2728/paper1.pdf</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#MasteryClimatePerceived">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gufo:IntrinsicMode representing an employee&apos;s perception that the team climate emphasizes learning, effort, collaboration, and personal improvement.

In the context of the OntoTurnover domain, this intrinsic mode inheres in an Employee (gufo:inheresIn) and is a potential employee-influenced retention factor. Its instances enter a EmployeeInfluencedRetentionContext through :isAspectualFactorOf, a subproperty of gufo:standsIn and :isContextualFactorOf, and are therefore classified by the reasoner as RetentionPotentialFactor. The context, not the factor itself, may contribute to triggering a StayIntentionFormation (gufo:contributedToTrigger), and the property chain :contributedToFormationOf infers the resulting intention when one is recorded. Being a factor does not entail that an intention, a decision, or a retention actually occurs.

Examples include an employee who feels that effort and learning are valued more than internal rankings.

Synonyms: Learning-Oriented Climate; Task-Involvement Climate; Mastery Environment Perceived; Mastery Atmosphere Perceived; Mastery Work Climate Perceived; Mastery Climate Subjective; Mastery Climate Experienced; Mastery Climate Perceived Level of.

References:

Enander, A., &amp; Cardoso, J. (2020). How is employee turnover related to employee retention? A systematic review on two sets of meta-analyses [Dissertação de mestrado, Lund University]. Lund University Publications. http://lup.lub.lu.se/student-papers/record/9022943/file/9022946.pdf

Almeida, J. P. A., Guizzardi, G., Sales, T. P., &amp; Falbo, R. A. (2019). gUFO: A Lightweight Implementation of the Unified Foundational Ontology (UFO). https://nemo-ufes.github.io/gufo/

