Guizzardi, R., Carneiro, B. G., Porello, D., &amp; Guizzardi, G. (2020). A core ontology on decision making. CEUR Workshop Proceedings, 2728, 9–21. https://ceur-ws.org/Vol-2728/paper1.pdf</rdfs:comment>
    </rdf:Description>
    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#MissedDeliveryDeadlines">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gufo:Situation representing a post-state in which organizational milestones or deadlines are missed due to lack of staff after voluntary exits.

In the context of the OntoTurnover domain, this post-state situation is a potential consequence of voluntary turnover for the employer. Its instances are elements of an EmployerVoluntaryTurnoverConsequenceContext through :isConsequenceElementOf (inverse :hasConsequenceElement), and that context is brought about (gufo:broughtAbout) by a VoluntaryTurnover. It is a contingent outcome whose presence, intensity, and duration vary across employees, employers, and employment settings.

Examples include a consultancy that misses a client milestone after two consultants resign.

Synonyms: missed deadlines; late delivery; delivery-date failure; deadline noncompliance; overdue delivery; delivery schedule slippage.

References:

Enander, A., &amp; Cardoso, J. (2020). How is employee turnover related to employee retention? A systematic review on two sets of meta-analyses [Dissertação de mestrado, Lund University]. Lund University Publications. http://lup.lub.lu.se/student-papers/record/9022943/file/9022946.pdf

