    <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/ontoturnover#NonMonetaryBenefits">
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A gufo:Situation representing a situation in which employees receive non-cash rewards, such as extra days off, education sponsorship, or wellness allowances.

In the context of the OntoTurnover domain, this situation is a potential employer-influenced retention factor. Its instances enter a EmployerInfluencedRetentionContext through :isSituationalFactorOf, a subproperty of gufo:isSituationProperPartOf and :isContextualFactorOf, and are therefore classified by the reasoner as RetentionPotentialFactor. The context, not the factor itself, may contribute to triggering a StayIntentionFormation (gufo:contributedToTrigger), and the property chain :contributedToFormationOf infers the resulting intention when one is recorded. Being a factor does not entail that an intention, a decision, or a retention actually occurs.

Examples include an employee who receives a paid day off on their birthday and a language course.

Synonyms: noncash benefits; fringe benefits; employee perks; indirect compensation; nonfinancial rewards; in-kind benefits.

References:

Enander, A., &amp; Cardoso, J. (2020). How is employee turnover related to employee retention? A systematic review on two sets of meta-analyses [Dissertação de mestrado, Lund University]. Lund University Publications. http://lup.lub.lu.se/student-papers/record/9022943/file/9022946.pdf

